Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:46:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 405/488] prepare_prefill, combine and the resampled token:
 Triton's shapes and loads

prepare_prefill_inputs takes Triton's four warps (eight tokens a thread,
loads and stores predicated): at decode every block exits at once, and
eight warps a block cost 0.1-0.3 us. Combine's index and input-id stores
are predicated instead of branching. The resampled token's warp loads
every block's maximum and id with the row, before the count, state and
temperature, and its reduction carries the winner's id, so the chain is
three rounds of loads, not five.
